{"type":"bullets","design":"ENGINE_BULLETS","title":"Platform limitations impacting delivery","lead":"Fragile data processing and scaling bottlenecks create operational risk across business services.","points":["Scaling ceilings: Fixed cluster capacities struggle to absorb sudden spikes in web-scraped and partner data feeds.","Query contention: Heavy background transformation jobs compete with customer-facing analytics for compute resources.","High maintenance overhead: Engineering teams spend excessive time troubleshooting broken pipelines rather than building new features.","Siloed data copies: Redundant data movement across staging environments increases storage costs and compliance exposure."],"callout":{"label":"Industry benchmark","title":"Engineering productivity gains","text":"According to Forrester, enterprises implementing a unified Google Cloud lakehouse with BigQuery, BigLake, and Dataplex boost data engineering productivity by 38% and data analyst productivity by 35% through simplified pipelines."},"notes":"Pipeline fragility and fixed capacity limits directly impact data freshness and engineering velocity. When upstream data sources change unexpectedly, manual intervention is required to restore service, putting availability targets at risk. By eliminating siloed data copies and manual cluster tuning on Google Cloud, enterprises in Forrester's study achieved a 38% boost in data engineering productivity and a 35% increase in data analyst productivity.

