{"type":"diagram","design":"","title":"ZoomInfo Google Cloud target architecture","lead":"An end-to-end serverless lakehouse built on Pub/Sub, Dataflow, BigQuery, BigLake, and Dataplex.","center":"Google Cloud lakehouse","text":"Unified platform for streaming ingestion, processing, storage, and governance.","items":[{"title":"Pub/Sub ingestion","text":"Global message bus ingesting real-time B2B events with durable multi-zone buffering.","icon":"cloud-upload"},{"title":"Dataflow processing","text":"Serverless Beam pipelines handling validation, enrichment, deduplication, and schemas.","icon":"workflow-path"},{"title":"BigQuery core storage","text":"Petabyte-scale analytical warehouse powering fast B2B queries with decoupled compute.","icon":"database"},{"title":"BigLake open format","text":"Storage engine extending BigQuery security and query acceleration across Cloud Storage.","icon":"cloud-layers"},{"title":"Dataplex governance","text":"Centralized fabric automating quality checks, lineage tracking, metadata, and PII policy.","icon":"shield-database"},{"title":"Cloud Composer orchestration","text":"Managed Airflow coordinating multi-step analytical jobs and cross-system SLAs.","icon":"gear-cycle"}],"notes":"The target architecture consolidates ZoomInfo's data estate onto Google Cloud's native lakehouse stack. Pub/Sub and Dataflow handle continuous event ingestion and stream processing, landing validated data into BigQuery and BigLake tables over Cloud Storage. Dataplex provides overarching governance and quality enforcement across all storage tiers, while Cloud Composer orchestrates complex cross-pipeline dependencies.

