{"type":"cards","design":"","title":"Data governance and PII compliance on Google Cloud","lead":"Centralized policy enforcement and automated PII discovery protect ZoomInfo B2B contact records.","items":[{"title":"Automated PII classification","text":"Sensitive Data Protection scans incoming B2B contact streams to identify, classify, and redact personal identifiers before records land in analytical tables, ensuring compliance with global privacy regulations.","icon":"search-user"},{"title":"Unified Dataplex governance","text":"Dataplex applies consistent data quality rules, lineage tracking, and access policies across Cloud Storage and BigQuery, giving data stewards a single control plane over all contact datasets.","icon":"shield-database"},{"title":"Fine-grained access control","text":"BigQuery policy tags enforce column-level security and dynamic data masking, ensuring engineering and analytics teams only view sensitive contact fields authorized for their specific role.","icon":"lock"},{"title":"Customer-managed encryption","text":"Cloud KMS customer-managed encryption keys and VPC Service Controls establish a cryptographic perimeter around ZoomInfo datasets, preventing unauthorized data exfiltration across project boundaries.","icon":"key"}],"notes":"ZoomInfo manages sensitive B2B contact and company data that requires strict regulatory compliance. By combining Dataplex with Sensitive Data Protection and BigQuery column-level security, ZoomInfo can centralize governance across its lakehouse while boosting engineering and analyst productivity.

