{"type":"process","design":"","title":"Query performance optimization process","lead":"A four-step engineering workflow profiles, restructures, and tunes workloads for sustained speed.","items":[{"title":"Execution graph profiling","text":"Analyze INFORMATION_SCHEMA job history and query execution graphs to identify slot contention, shuffle bottlenecks, and full-table scans across legacy queries. This pinpoints the costliest resource drains for remediation.","icon":"magnifying-glass"},{"title":"Schema and key restructuring","text":"Redesign target tables using nested and repeated fields to eliminate expensive self-joins while applying partition and cluster keys aligned to query predicates. Denormalizing structures accelerates complex operational queries.","icon":"wrench"},{"title":"Smart materialization","text":"Deploy automated materialized views with query rewrite enabled so BigQuery pre-computes common B2B contact aggregations and serves results directly. Underlying queries bypass base tables entirely to accelerate responses.","icon":"database"},{"title":"Autonomous runtime tuning","text":"Enable BigQuery history-based optimizations and CMETA metadata indexing to dynamically adjust join strategies and slot concurrency without manual intervention. Execution engines continuously adapt based on prior runtime metrics.","icon":"gear-chart"}],"notes":"Our optimization process moves systematically from profiling to autonomous tuning. After restructuring schemas and deploying materialized views, we enable BigQuery's history-based optimizer and CMETA metadata foundation, which Google Cloud benchmarks show can reduce query latencies without manual DBA tuning.

